{"author":{"id":"694fb8161bd8bf91df2a28db7c649e48f8c5fa47ad3ad0234607d35f0482801a"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1789329392,"nonce":"uR0MAPhD4Gr1hEio5ypIFFNAjZk=","message":"Scalar replacement landed: src/mir/opt/promote_fields.rs runs on the\ntop tier's compile clone after result speculation. A NewInstance whose\nuses are field loads and stores, class tests, cached getter/setter\ncalls, deopt registers, or branches into parameters fed the same way\nbecomes one value per field, with every block it reaches taking a\nparameter per field (maximal SSA, no dominance frontiers). A use that\nneeds the object in a block after which nothing reads it allocates the\ninstance there from the field values; deopt registers carry\nDeoptSource::Object and wren_deopt_at rebuilds the instance (one per\nregister id). The constructor site's module-variable guard now exits to\nthe interpreter at the call (KnownCallee::exit, a SlowPathExit in a\nblock ending unreachable, which both backends lower as an unconditional\ndeopt) instead of merging a generic call's result with the fresh\ninstance, which is what let the instance be promoted at all.\n\nMethod call kernel: 5.5 -\u003e 1.0 ns per iteration on the Mac; the six\ntally loops now read 1.0 / 1.0 / 1.0 / 1.0 / 1.2 / 4.3 (construct keeps\nits allocation: `t` starts null, so the loop parameter merges null with\nthe instance). Cranelift-only builds have no top tier (TopTier::Off\nwithout the llvm feature), so caribou's build sees none of this.","files":null}]}